{
  "name": "iso42001",
  "annotations": [
    {
      "tag": "standard",
      "value": "ISO/IEC 42001:2023"
    },
    {
      "tag": "edition",
      "value": "1"
    },
    {
      "tag": "publication_date",
      "value": "2023-12-18"
    },
    {
      "tag": "normative_reference",
      "value": "ISO/IEC 22989:2022"
    },
    {
      "tag": "iso_open_data_date",
      "value": "2026-11-05"
    }
  ],
  "description": "A LinkML model of the records an organization keeps to run an artificial intelligence (AI) management system under ISO/IEC 42001:2023. The records cover its context, leadership, planning and support, how it weighs and treats AI risks, and what its AI systems may do to people and society. They also cover those systems with their resources, data and documents, its audits and reviews, and what it corrects and improves. The reference controls of Annex A appear by number, with titles of this project's own.",
  "title": "ISO/IEC 42001:2023 AI management system records",
  "comments": [
    "The version is the edition the schema models, and source is ISO's page for it. ISO Open Data's records of the edition and of its normative reference are copied to src/iso42001/schema/iso-open-data/ on the date the annotations give, and scripts/check_upstream_release.py reports when ISO changes them. The release tags are the schema's own versions.",
    "ISO/IEC 42001 is copyright ISO and IEC, and none of its text is reproduced here. An element cites what it models by number, in the iso42001_clause, annex_a_control, annex_b_item, annex_c_item or annex_d_item annotation, and its title and description are this project's own words. A reader with a licensed copy looks the text up by that number, and a record's title and description hold the organization's own words.",
    "The terms follow ISO/IEC 22989:2022, the one normative reference, and so do the stages of a system's life and the kinds of AI role. Annexes C and D are informative and give examples, so an enum built from one of them has the value other.",
    "Every record that other records refer to has an aims_id, and a reference holds that identifier. AimsManagementSystem holds each kind of record in a list of its own.",
    "A close mapping to lmodel/iso27001 names the class that answers to the same clause number, since both standards follow the harmonized structure of management system standards. AimsOrganization and AimsRole are the same kind of thing as SPDX's Organization and OSCAL's Role. AimsControl is related to OSCAL's Control: both name a safeguard, but OSCAL's is a catalogue entry and this one is the organization's own."
  ],
  "source": "https://www.iso.org/standard/81230.html",
  "see_also": [
    "https://lmodel.github.io/iso42001",
    "https://www.iso.org/standard/81230.html",
    "https://www.iso.org/standard/74296.html"
  ],
  "id": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001",
  "version": "2023",
  "imports": [
    "linkml:types"
  ],
  "license": "Apache-2.0",
  "prefixes": [
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "linkml",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/linkml/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "iso42001",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "iso27001",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso27001/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "oscal",
      "prefix_reference": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/oscal/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "schema",
      "prefix_reference": "http://schema.org/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "spdx_core",
      "prefix_reference": "https://spdx.org/rdf/3.0.1/terms/Core/"
    },
    {
      "prefix_prefix": "xsd",
      "prefix_reference": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#"
    }
  ],
  "default_prefix": "iso42001",
  "default_range": "string",
  "subsets": [
    {
      "name": "aims_core",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001/AimsCore",
      "description": "The records of the system's context, leadership, planning and support (clauses 4 to 7).",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001",
      "@type": "SubsetDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "aims_risk_management",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001/AimsRiskManagement",
      "description": "The records of risk assessment, risk treatment and impact assessment (clauses 6.1, 8.2, 8.3 and 8.4).",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001",
      "@type": "SubsetDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "aims_annex_a",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001/AimsAnnexA",
      "description": "The Annex A reference controls, the organization's own controls and the Statement of Applicability.",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001",
      "@type": "SubsetDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "aims_ai_systems",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001/AimsAiSystems",
      "description": "The AI systems, their resources, data and documents, and what is told to those who use or depend on them (Annex A, areas A.4 and A.6 to A.9).",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001",
      "@type": "SubsetDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "aims_external_parties",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001/AimsExternalParties",
      "description": "The relationships with partners, suppliers and customers (Annex A, area A.10).",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001",
      "@type": "SubsetDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "aims_performance_evaluation",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001/AimsPerformanceEvaluation",
      "description": "The records of monitoring, internal audit and management review (clause 9).",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001",
      "@type": "SubsetDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "aims_improvement",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001/AimsImprovement",
      "description": "The records of getting better: improvements, nonconformities and what corrects them (clause 10).",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001",
      "@type": "SubsetDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "aims_documented_information",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001/AimsDocumentedInformation",
      "description": "The records that are documented information under document control (clause 7.5).",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001",
      "@type": "SubsetDefinition"
    }
  ],
  "types": [
    {
      "name": "aims_duration",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001/AimsDuration",
      "description": "A length of time as ISO 8601 writes it, such as P7Y for seven years or P30D for thirty days.",
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/iso42001",
      "typeof": "string",
      "base": "str",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#duration",
      "pattern": "^P(?=[0-9T])([0-9]+Y)?([0-9]+M)?([0-9]+W)?([0-9]+D)?(T(?=[0-9])([0-9]+H)?([0-9]+M)?([0-9]+S)?)?$",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "string",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/linkml/String",
      "description": "A character string",
      "notes": [
        "In RDF serializations, a slot with range of string is treated as a literal or type xsd:string. If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"string\"."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/linkml/types",
      "imported_from": "linkml:types",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "schema:Text"
      ],
      "base": "str",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "integer",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/linkml/Integer",
      "description": "An integer",
      "notes": [
        "If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"integer\"."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/linkml/types",
      "imported_from": "linkml:types",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "schema:Integer"
      ],
      "base": "int",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "boolean",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/linkml/Boolean",
      "description": "A binary (true or false) value",
      "notes": [
        "If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"boolean\"."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/linkml/types",
      "imported_from": "linkml:types",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "schema:Boolean"
      ],
      "base": "Bool",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean",
      "repr": "bool",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "float",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/linkml/Float",
      "description": "A real number that conforms to the xsd:float specification",
      "notes": [
        "If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"float\"."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/linkml/types",
      "imported_from": "linkml:types",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "schema:Float"
      ],
      "base": "float",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#float",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "double",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/linkml/Double",
      "description": "A real number that conforms to the xsd:double specification",
      "notes": [
        "If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"double\"."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/linkml/types",
      "imported_from": "linkml:types",
      "close_mappings": [
        "schema:Float"
      ],
      "base": "float",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "decimal",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/linkml/Decimal",
      "description": "A real number with arbitrary precision that conforms to the xsd:decimal specification",
      "notes": [
        "If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"decimal\"."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/linkml/types",
      "imported_from": "linkml:types",
      "broad_mappings": [
        "schema:Number"
      ],
      "base": "Decimal",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "time",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/linkml/Time",
      "description": "A time object represents a (local) time of day, independent of any particular day",
      "notes": [
        "URI is dateTime because OWL reasoners do not work with straight date or time",
        "If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"time\"."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/linkml/types",
      "imported_from": "linkml:types",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "schema:Time"
      ],
      "base": "XSDTime",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#time",
      "repr": "str",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
    {
      "name": "date",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/linkml/Date",
      "description": "a date (year, month and day) in an idealized calendar",
      "notes": [
        "URI is dateTime because OWL reasoners don't work with straight date or time",
        "If you are authoring schemas in LinkML YAML, the type is referenced with the lower case \"date\"."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/linkml/types",
      "imported_from": "linkml:types",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "schema:Date"
      ],
      "base": "XSDDate",
      "uri": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date",
      "repr": "str",
      "@type": "TypeDefinition"
    },
    {
